   Here's the deal with artifacts...  you can wish for them, but if they are
not specifically for your class, you will take damage whenever you touch (i.e.
pick up or wield/wear) them.  However, if your alignment is different, it won't
let you use it at all.  The only way to have access to all of them is to get a
blessed +whatever helm of opposite alignment.  Each time you put it on, it'll
change you to another alignment (most useful with neutral characters, as they
can then become any one of the three).  My 15th level wizard has the Eye of
Aeopithica and the Staff of Aesculapius (a nifty weapon, indeed), in addition
to all his other artifact weapons (Vorpal Blade, Magic Bane, Fire Brand). 
Neutral characters can also use the Heart of Ahriman and the Orb of Fate
without much harm (just the occasional shock) and a quick tip of the hat allows
you to switch to an alignment that lets you use anything else.

